# Trivy accepted-risk exceptions for deploy/Dockerfile.server and
# deploy/Dockerfile.worker (security-image job, .github/workflows/ci.yml).
#
# Empty by design: no exception has been reviewed/accepted yet. Do not add a
# CVE id here to silence a scan failure without following the same
# "documented exception" discipline as deny.toml / docs/adr/TEMPLATE.md's
# "Exception lifecycle" section:
#   - one line per accepted CVE/advisory id
#   - a trailing `#` comment naming: owner, why it cannot be fixed now, and an
#     expiry/retest date (Trivy also supports an inline `exp:YYYY-MM-DD` after
#     the id to auto-expire the ignore)
#
# Example (uncomment and edit, do not leave unattributed):
#   CVE-2025-NNNNN exp:2026-09-01  # owner: <name> — base-image fix not yet
#     released upstream, retest at next debian:bookworm-slim digest bump.
